    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0413" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100 K77/9.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Cuba to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Cuba</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washing</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I beg to acknowledge
                    receipt of your favor of the 13th instant,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d422-f1"/> in
                    which you state that the Honorable President has directed the Honorable
                    Secretary of State to visit [etc.]</p>
                <p>I note with great satisfaction the expression of the Secretary’s anticipations as
                    regards his visit to Cuba and his sentiments and those of the United States
                    towards my country; and I can assure you that my Government and the people of
                    Cuba will gladly improve the opportunity now offered them to show Secretary Knox
                    their high appreciation of his personality and his friendly interest in Cuba,
                    and also the warm friendship of my country towards the United States.</p>
                <p>I beg to remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Antonio Martin Rivero</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d422-f1" n="1" xml:id="d422-f1-content">
                <p>The identic letter printed under Panama, “Visit of the Secretary of State to the
                    Republics of Central America and the Caribbean Sea,” <ref target="#pg1240">p.
                        1240</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
